 (109). Homer's all-time high is 81\u00b0F, on July 10, 1993.","t_chg":"Homer has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 86 complete years: Homer's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.54\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.36 to +0.72), about +4.9\u00b0F since 1933. Homer's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.34\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.51), about +3.1\u00b0F since 1933.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Homer's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.06 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 23.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1981 (38.10 in); the driest, 1996 (12.95 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}